            "readable_text": "We have a product of a negative number [MATH: ({\\color{red}-5})] and a positive number [MATH: ({\\color{blue}2}).] So the product will be negative:\n[MATH: 10]\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply [MATH: 5] by [MATH: 2] without any signs: [MATH: 5 \\cdot 2 = 10.] So, we get\n\n[MATH: {\\color{red}(-5)} \\cdot {\\color{blue}2} = {\\color{red}-10}.]",
